  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Bulakba\u015f\u0131, sometimes Ba\u015fbulak ARM</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Ba\u015fbulak/Bulakba\u015f\u0131/Kan\u00ee Kewang is situated near Ta\u015fburun in the Kars province in eastern Turkey. Here a stone block with an inscription of the Urartian king Minua (9th / 8th century BCE) was found, in which he claims to have built the building to which the stone block belonged. Furthermore, Minua states that he has built a fortress at this place and given it the name \"Minuahinili\". In Roman times, the locality was known as Paracata.",
